# Story page: brick
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Chipped Brick
---
A brick from the Old Yard, chipped at one corner and carved with a snake in the act of biting its own tail.

The carving is old. It is older than the yard, older than the bricks around it, and older, I am beginning to suspect, than the idea of bricks.

Scratched on the back, in letters smaller than a grain of rice: IF YOU ARE READING THIS, YOU HAVE BEEN HERE BEFORE. {name} decided not to think about it. I have thought about nothing else.
